1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,591
Hi Jeannie.

2
00:00:00,591 --> 00:00:01,550
How's it going?

3
00:00:01,550 --> 00:00:02,547
Oh, hello Dan.

4
00:00:02,547 --> 00:00:03,544
Pretty well, thanks.

5
00:00:03,544 --> 00:00:07,200
Have you managed to get the money for the course yet?

6
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:07,597
Yes,

7
00:00:07,597 --> 00:00:09,977
that's all sorted out now, thanks.

8
00:00:09,977 --> 00:00:11,960
It took long enough, though.

9
00:00:11,960 --> 00:00:15,783
It was practically a year ago that I applied to my local council for

10
00:00:15,783 --> 00:00:16,329
a grant,

11
00:00:16,329 --> 00:00:19,060
and it took them six months to turn me down.

12
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:20,940
That's really slow.

13
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:23,952
And I thought I was eligible for government funding,

14
00:00:23,952 --> 00:00:25,960
but it seems I was mistaken.

15
00:00:25,960 --> 00:00:29,973
So then I asked the boss of the company I used to work for

16
00:00:29,973 --> 00:00:31,407
if they would sponsor me,

17
00:00:31,407 --> 00:00:34,560
and much to my surprise, he said they'd make a contribution.

18
00:00:34,560 --> 00:00:37,220
But what about college grants and scholarships?

19
00:00:37,220 --> 00:00:40,260
There must be some you could apply for.

20
00:00:40,260 --> 00:00:41,157
Yes, there are,

21
00:00:41,157 --> 00:00:45,341
but they're all so small that I decided to leave them until I was

22
00:00:45,341 --> 00:00:45,640
desperate.

23
00:00:45,640 --> 00:00:46,200
Uhuh.

24
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:48,620
And in fact I didn't need to apply.

25
00:00:48,620 --> 00:00:52,975
My parents had been saying that as I already had a job, I ought

26
00:00:52,975 --> 00:00:54,530
to support myself through college.

27
00:00:54,530 --> 00:00:57,269
But in the end they took pity on me,

28
00:00:57,269 --> 00:00:59,400
so now I've just about got enough.

29
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:00,350
That's good.

30
00:01:00,350 --> 00:01:05,998
So now I can put a bit of effort into meeting people - I haven't had time

31
00:01:05,998 --> 00:01:06,704
so far.

32
00:01:06,704 --> 00:01:07,410
Any suggestions?

33
00:01:07,410 --> 00:01:10,430
What about joining some college clubs?

34
00:01:10,430 --> 00:01:11,136
Oh right.

35
00:01:11,136 --> 00:01:12,900
You joined several didn't you?

36
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:15,202
Yes, I'm in the drama club.

37
00:01:15,202 --> 00:01:17,504
It's our first performance next week,

38
00:01:17,504 --> 00:01:19,039
so we're rehearsing frantically,

39
00:01:19,039 --> 00:01:21,725
and I've got behind with my work,

40
00:01:21,725 --> 00:01:23,260
but it's worth it.

41
00:01:23,260 --> 00:01:26,420
I'm hoping to be in the spring production, too.

42
00:01:26,420 --> 00:01:27,936
I've never liked acting.

43
00:01:27,936 --> 00:01:29,830
Are you doing anything else?

44
00:01:29,830 --> 00:01:32,048
I enjoyed singing when I was at school,

45
00:01:32,048 --> 00:01:34,820
so I joined a group when I came to college.

46
00:01:34,820 --> 00:01:39,267
I don't think the conductor stretches us enough, though so I'll give up after

47
00:01:39,267 --> 00:01:40,220
the next concert.

48
00:01:40,220 --> 00:01:42,885
And I also joined the debating society.

49
00:01:42,885 --> 00:01:43,647
It's fun,

50
00:01:43,647 --> 00:01:47,835
but with all the rehearsing I'm doing, something has to go,

51
00:01:47,835 --> 00:01:50,120
and I'm afraid that's the one.

52
00:01:50,120 --> 00:01:51,730
Do you do any sports?

53
00:01:51,730 --> 00:01:54,118
Yes, I'm in one of the hockey teams.

54
00:01:54,118 --> 00:01:55,312
I'm not very good,

55
00:01:55,312 --> 00:01:57,700
but I'd really miss it if I stopped.

56
00:01:57,700 --> 00:02:01,282
I decided to try tennis when I came to college,

57
00:02:01,282 --> 00:02:03,789
and I'm finding it pretty tough going.

58
00:02:03,789 --> 00:02:05,580
I'm simply not fit enough.

59
00:02:05,580 --> 00:02:06,120
Nor me.

60
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:08,010
I think I'll give that a miss!

61
00:02:08,010 --> 00:02:10,992
I'm hoping it'll help me to build up my stamina,

62
00:02:10,992 --> 00:02:13,080
but it'll probably be a long haul.

63
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:13,730
Good luck.

64
00:02:13,730 --> 00:02:14,500
Thanks.

65
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:16,320
How are you finding the course?

66
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:19,000
I wish we had more seminars.

67
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:19,361
What?

68
00:02:19,361 --> 00:02:22,610
I'd have thought we had more than enough already.

69
00:02:22,610 --> 00:02:27,194
All those people saying clever things that I could never think of- it's quite

70
00:02:27,194 --> 00:02:27,521
interesting,

71
00:02:27,521 --> 00:02:31,450
but I wonder if I'm clever enough to be doing this course.

72
00:02:31,450 --> 00:02:34,210
I find it helpful to listen to the other people.

73
00:02:34,210 --> 00:02:37,271
I like the way we're exploring the subject,

74
00:02:37,271 --> 00:02:39,950
and working towards getting insight into it.

75
00:02:39,950 --> 00:02:42,364
How do you get on with your tutor?

76
00:02:42,364 --> 00:02:45,381
I don't think I'm on the same wavelength as mine,

77
00:02:45,381 --> 00:02:48,700
so I feel I'm not getting anything out of the tutorials.

78
00:02:48,700 --> 00:02:51,700
It would be more productive to read a book instead.

79
00:02:51,700 --> 00:02:53,190
Oh, mine's very demanding.

80
00:02:53,190 --> 00:02:56,170
She gives me lots of feedback and advice,

81
00:02:56,170 --> 00:02:59,150
so I've got much better at writing essays.

82
00:02:59,150 --> 00:03:02,940
And she's helping me plan my revision for the end-of-year exams.

83
00:03:02,940 --> 00:03:05,270
Do tell me, I always struggle with revision.

84
00:03:05,270 --> 00:03:11,840
Well, the first thing is to find out exactly what's required in the exams.

85
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:12,165
Mm.

86
00:03:12,165 --> 00:03:15,420
Would it help to get hold of some past papers?

87
00:03:15,420 --> 00:03:15,781
Yes.

88
00:03:15,781 --> 00:03:17,950
They'll help to make it clear.

89
00:03:17,950 --> 00:03:19,503
Right, I'll do that.

90
00:03:19,503 --> 00:03:20,280
Then what?

91
00:03:20,280 --> 00:03:24,629
Then you can sort out your revision priorities, based on what's most likely to

92
00:03:24,629 --> 00:03:25,250
come up.

93
00:03:25,250 --> 00:03:26,946
I put these on a card,

94
00:03:26,946 --> 00:03:28,360
and read them through regularly.

95
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:28,920
Uhuh.

96
00:03:28,920 --> 00:03:30,730
But that isn't enough in itself.

97
00:03:30,730 --> 00:03:34,955
You also need a timetable, to see how you can fit everything in, in

98
00:03:34,955 --> 00:03:35,860
the time available.

99
00:03:35,860 --> 00:03:38,800
Then keep it in front of you while you're studying.

100
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:40,000
I've done that before,

101
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:41,500
but it hasn't helped me!

102
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:44,336
Maybe you need to do something different every day,

103
00:03:44,336 --> 00:03:47,488
so if you break down your revision into small tasks,

104
00:03:47,488 --> 00:03:51,270
and allocate them to specific days, there's more incentive to tackle them.

105
00:03:51,270 --> 00:03:54,800
With big topics you're more likely to put off starting.

106
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:56,060
Good idea.

107
00:03:56,060 --> 00:04:00,234
And as I revise each topic I write a single paragraph about it -

108
00:04:00,234 --> 00:04:02,481
then later can read it through quickly,

109
00:04:02,481 --> 00:04:05,050
and it helps fix things in my mind.

110
00:04:05,050 --> 00:04:06,200
That's brilliant.

111
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:09,300
I also write answers to questions for the exam practice.

112
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:11,780
It's hard to make myself do it, though!

113
00:04:11,780 --> 00:04:13,155
Well, I'll try.

114
00:04:13,155 --> 00:04:14,987
Thanks a lot, Jeannie.

115
00:04:14,987 --> 00:04:16,820
That's a great help.

116
00:04:16,820 --> 00:04:17,600
No problem.

117
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:18,700
See you around.

118
00:04:18,700 --> 00:04:19,500
Bye.
